WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.220
For all the answers we got at the end of Endgame,
there are still a few nagging questions that

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.630
weren't entirely summed up by the time those
credits rolled.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:13.190
Some of these questions go back multiple films
in the franchise, while others were introduced

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:15.920
in Endgame and then seemingly abandoned.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.370
What are we talking about?

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:22.010
Snap on your spoiler gloves, because we're
digging deep to find all the unanswered questions

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.039
from Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.360
Once again, to be clear: Spoilers ahead!

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:32.720
There was a lot of mantle passing in the closing
moments of Endgame, much of it in heartwarming

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:33.730
fashion.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.149
Old Man Cap passing his shield on to Falcon?

00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:38.110
It doesn't get much better than that.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:42.470
We've got a more grown-up Cassie Lang in the
picture, and Clint hit a bullseye with his

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:43.470
daughter.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:44.700
But what about Iron Man?

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.329
Who's set to replace him?

00:00:46.329 --> 00:00:49.820
The obvious choice is, of course, little Morgan
Stark.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:53.540
Her father even died in a battle with an intergalactic
wacko.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.070
Stuff that in a box and label it "Origin Story."

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:00.630
But if that's the timeline the MCU is taking,
it raises the question: When is the next time

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:03.469
we'll see a version of Iron Man on the big
screen?

00:01:03.469 --> 00:01:05.610
Morgan's, what, four years old?

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.270
Less than five for sure, because of the snappenings.

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:12.100
By the time she's old enough to strap on some
nanites, the rest of the Avengers will be

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.400
hanging up their own suits.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.000
Months before Endgame's release, a theory
was making the rounds that Tony Stark would

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.540
make his own Infinity Gauntlet and reverse
Thanos' snap.

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:26.830
It didn't happen quite like that, but the
theory was pretty dang close, and it brought

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:31.259
up some really interesting points that we
were all hoping would get answered in Endgame.

00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:36.010
One is the idea that Tony has been feeling
echoes across time from using the Stones.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:39.799
Across several movies, Tony Stark has been
having problems with his arm.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:44.450
If he had such immense power at his fingertips,
some of that power might ripple backwards

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:49.430
through time and give him arm problems as
far back as Captain America: Civil War.

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:52.530
But Infinity War brought that ripple even
closer to home.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:56.860
Remember how Tony Stark had a dream that Pepper
had a baby girl and they named her Morgan?

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:00.990
A dream like that could have been another
echo from the future, since future Tony knew

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:03.920
that he had a daughter when he used the Infinity
Stones.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.590
And its placement in the film just before
Endgame has to be more than coincidence.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.200
"Future uses, and that's it.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.960
Just in case there's a monster in the closet
instead of, you know…"

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.480
"Shirts."

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:19.680
Unfortunately, it's all still just speculation,
since Endgame never really addressed that

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.000
in any way.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.599
Infinity War's big thing was unquestionably
the snap.

00:02:25.599 --> 00:02:30.120
Thanos foreshadowed it, then the final battle
came and he upheld his promise, turning half

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.949
the universe to dust with a snap of his fingers.

00:02:32.949 --> 00:02:35.080
Cinematically, it's great.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:40.080
It's one instantly identifiable gesture of
annihilation that also says, "Look how easy

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.960
it is to clean up the universe."

00:02:46.969 --> 00:02:51.240
From a comics perspective, it holds up as
well, since that's what Thanos did in Infinity

00:02:51.249 --> 00:02:52.249
Gauntlet.

00:02:52.249 --> 00:02:57.239
So then Endgame comes along, and the only
way to make the Stones work is now snapping.

00:02:57.239 --> 00:02:59.069
Is that in the Infinity Manual?

00:02:59.069 --> 00:03:03.089
When Professor Hulk put on the glove the first
time, he was clearly picturing what he wanted

00:03:03.089 --> 00:03:06.689
to happen, since he says he also tried to
bring back Natasha.

00:03:06.689 --> 00:03:10.109
And in the final battle, both Tony and Thanos
try snapping.

00:03:10.109 --> 00:03:14.879
The movie never answers the question of whether
there are other ways to use all the Stones.

00:03:14.879 --> 00:03:18.629
After all, if they're powerful enough to bring
back trillions of life forms with all their

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:23.720
memories and costumes intact, wouldn't just
wishing be enough without the snap?

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:29.280
Let's face it: Any movie dealing with time
travel is going to run into problems.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:33.689
For its part, though, Endgame did wrap up
a lot of loose timelines, explain most of

00:03:33.689 --> 00:03:36.639
what needed explaining, and keep the plot
moving.

00:03:36.639 --> 00:03:41.239
Out of all the time travel shenanigans, one
question that was almost definitely intentionally

00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:45.069
left unanswered was the 2012 Loki's whereabouts.

00:03:45.069 --> 00:03:49.849
If you remember, while in the past after the
Battle of New York, Stark fumbled the Tesseract,

00:03:49.849 --> 00:03:53.839
and Loki snagged it while no one was looking
and slipped away into a portal.

00:03:53.839 --> 00:03:58.749
By doing so, he presumably created a different
timeline that didn't end up with that version

00:03:58.749 --> 00:04:01.049
of himself being choked by Thanos.

00:04:01.049 --> 00:04:05.489
So now there's a rogue Loki roaming another
timeline, but the movie leaves that guy's

00:04:05.489 --> 00:04:07.489
fate completely unmentioned.

00:04:07.489 --> 00:04:11.200
What kind of mischief is he getting up to
with the ability to travel anywhere in the

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.200
universe?

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:15.079
"I'm sorry about that thing with the Tesseract.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:17.080
I just couldn't help myself."

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:21.280
There's a huge disconnect between the way
the Infinity Stones are built up in the previous

00:04:21.299 --> 00:04:23.990
movies, and the way they're handled in Endgame.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:25.389
Literally handled.

00:04:25.389 --> 00:04:29.199
In Guardians of the Galaxy, the Collector
gave a whole Powerpoint presentation that

00:04:29.199 --> 00:04:33.360
explained how only a being of extraordinary
strength can wield an Infinity Stone.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:38.580
A few seconds later, his lady servant grabbed
the Power Stone and exploded to prove to audiences

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.080
that he wasn't lying.

00:04:44.449 --> 00:04:47.320
So sure, using the stones is devastating.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:50.770
But it's pretty clear what these stones can
do to you just by touching them.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:55.419
Fast forward to the Endgame, though, and people
are tossing the stones around like hot potatoes.

00:04:55.419 --> 00:04:59.540
For starters, Hulk and Hawkeye both held a
Stone in their bare hands.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.910
Granted, those are plausible, at least.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:05.300
The Hulk is, if nothing else, a being of immense
power.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:09.690
And just like Thanos, Clint Barton was given
the Soul Stone in exchange for his sacrifice,

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:12.340
so maybe he was allowed to hold it.

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:16.650
Even so, it's not like the Stones in the gauntlet
are shielded by anything, and yet half the

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:19.600
Avengers got in on that game of keep-away
with the glove.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:23.039
None of those mortals even brushed a finger
across an Infinity Stone?

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:27.040
None of them caught it wrong, or slapped a
palm over a Reality Stone or two?

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:33.000
When Peter Parker comes back during that epic
final battle, he tells Tony that he must have

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:36.800
"passed out," because when he woke up back
on Titan, Stark was gone.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:40.889
The implication there is that time didn't
pass for the people who were dusted.

00:05:40.889 --> 00:05:44.530
Five years went by in the real world, but
all the dust bunnies came back just thinking

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:45.759
they'd taken a quick nap.

00:05:45.759 --> 00:05:50.280
It goes by pretty smoothly, mainly because
there's so much other stuff happening then,

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:54.219
but during the wrap-up scenes when we see
Peter back in school, reuniting with Ned,

00:05:54.219 --> 00:05:58.610
you start to wonder: How is society going
to reconcile what happened?

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:02.800
It's convenient that all of Peter's friends
were apparently also dusted, so now they get

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.620
to finish going through high school together.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.820
But what about the rest of the world?

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:10.610
Most of these people essentially blinked,
and Citi Field looks suddenly looks like the

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:11.669
apocalypse.

00:06:11.669 --> 00:06:13.210
Little Suzy's in college.

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:14.749
Grandpa Joe's kidneys failed.

00:06:14.749 --> 00:06:15.749
He's dead.

00:06:15.749 --> 00:06:18.430
Picture that, but multiplied by billions.

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:22.759
The world is going to have a whole heck of
a lot of work to do fixing things up, and

00:06:22.759 --> 00:06:25.039
Endgame didn't touch on that question at all.

00:06:25.039 --> 00:06:30.560
Finally, the most important question of all
is, who DOES put mayo on a hot dog?

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:31.560
Gross.

